$[Import* std]
Where a local definition shadows an outer `g`, the two forms differ (spec §2.4). The outer `g`:
$[# {g x} 10]
The plain form's expression cannot see the binding it makes, so it wraps the outer `g`.
${{^ {y} [# g {^ {x} {+ {g x} 1}}] {g y}} 1}
expect: 11
In a function definition, `g` is the new function itself: it counts down instead of calling the outer `g`.
${{^ {y} [# {g n} {!if {= n 0} 100 {g {- n 1}}}] {g y}} 3}
expect: 100
